            <ArticleTitle>A clinical approach to exercise tolerance testing in coronary artery disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>345-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Data from exercise tolerance testing should be incorporated into clinical decision making. A strategy for stratification of individual patients into high, indeterminate, and low-risk categories using Bruce protocol exercise testing is outlined. This approach will help to ensure further evaluation of high-risk individuals without excessive testing of patients having excellent long-term prognoses.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
